    body: "Conceived by former GM executive John Z. DeLorean as an ethical, long-lasting sports car, the DMC-12 is one of the most unconventional vehicles of the 20th century. Designed by Italdesign's Giorgetto Giugiaro, the car featured a fiberglass underbody wrapped in unpainted, brushed **SS304 stainless steel sheet metal**.\n\nCounterbalanced gullwing doors lifted effortlessly via cryogenically preset torsion bars, allowing entry in tight parking spaces with just 11 inches of clearance.\n\n![1981 DeLorean DMC-12 with Gullwing Doors Open | Picture courtesy of DeLorean Motor Company](/images/vehicles/1981-delorean-dmc-12.jpg)\n\nPowered by a rear-mounted 2.85L Peugeot-Renault-Volvo (PRV) V6, the car was elevated to global cinematic legend when it starred as Doc Brown's plutonium-powered time machine in *Back to the Future*.",
