    excerpt: "BMW's new M5 Touring combines a twin-turbo V8 with an electric motor for 727 hp. We test whether the formula still works on the Autobahn.",
    body: "The BMW M5 Touring represents something increasingly rare in the automotive world: a full-fat, high-performance station wagon with an unapologetic twin-turbo V8 at its core.\n\nPaired with a plug-in hybrid electric motor integrated into the 8-speed M Steptronic transmission, the M5 Touring delivers a combined **727 HP and 1,000 Nm of torque**.\n\n![BMW G99 M5 Touring on German Autobahn | Picture courtesy of BMW M GmbH](/images/vehicles/bmw-m5-touring.jpg)\n\n## Autobahn Supremacy Meets 500 Liters of Cargo\n\n0 to 100 km/h takes just 3.5 seconds, and with the optional M Driver's Package, the Touring will power continuously to 305 km/h (189 mph).\n\n- **Electric Commuting:** 18.6 kWh battery provides up to 69 km of emissions-free pure electric city driving.\n- **Chassis Control:** Standard adaptive M suspension with active roll stabilization disguises its 2,430 kg curb weight.\n- **Cargo Volume:** 500 liters expanding to 1,630 liters with rear seats folded.\n\nIt is an engineering tour-de-force that provides supercar theater with family usability.",
