    title: "How BYD Plans to Take 30% of Europe's EV Market by 2027",
    excerpt: "China's largest EV maker is building factories, slashing prices, and hiring thousands across Europe. Here's the playbook.",
    body: "BYD isn't just entering Europe—it's executing a multi-billion euro localized manufacturing strategy. With construction underway on its high-tech assembly facility in Szeged, Hungary and expansion into Turkey, BYD aims to insulate itself from EU import tariffs while providing rapid deliveries.\n\n![BYD Seal Electric Sedan at European Showroom | Picture courtesy of BYD Europe](/images/vehicles/byd-seal-excellence.jpg)\n\n## The Blade Battery Advantage\n\nBYD's structural **Blade Battery** (Lithium Iron Phosphate / LFP) forms an integral structural member of the CTB (Cell-to-Body) platform, delivering exceptional safety during nail-penetration tests and long-term durability at highly competitive pricing.\n\nWith models ranging from the sub-€25k Dolphin to the 530 hp Seal sedan, European legacy automakers are accelerating their own low-cost EV development in response.",
