    body: "Sharing Volkswagen Group's J1 high-performance 800V architecture, the Porsche Taycan 4S and Audi RS e-tron GT represent two divergent expressions of the ultimate electric grand tourer.\n\n![Porsche Taycan 4S vs Audi RS e-tron GT | Picture courtesy of Porsche Newsroom / Audi MediaCenter](/images/vehicles/audi-etron-gt.jpg)\n\n## Dynamic Precision vs Long-Distance Serenity\n\n- **Taycan 4S:** Laser-focused steering, lower seating position, firmer damping, and superior cornering rotation.\n- **RS e-tron GT:** Plump air suspension compliance, quieter cabin insulation, physical climate buttons, and muscular grand touring aesthetics.\n- **Charging:** Both charge at up to 270 kW, adding 100 km in 5 minutes.\n\nIf you carve alpine passes on weekends, pick the Taycan. If you devour 1,000 km cross-country road trips in serene luxury, the Audi is unbeatable.",
