    id: "a6",
    slug: "ford-maverick-hybrid-review",
    title: "Ford Maverick Hybrid: A Year Later, Still the Smartest Buy?",
    excerpt: "Over 42 mpg in city driving, genuine pickup truck utility, and an affordable price tag. We review our 20,000-mile long-term Maverick.",
    body: "In a world of $60,000 pickups, the compact Ford Maverick Hybrid remains one of the most rational and practical vehicles on the market.\n\n![Ford Maverick Hybrid Pickup Truck | Picture courtesy of Ford Motor Company](/images/vehicles/ford-maverick-hybrid.jpg)\n\nWith a 2.5-liter Atkinson-cycle hybrid powertrain averaging 42 mpg in town and a versatile 4.5-foot FLEXBED, the Maverick proves that compact utility doesn't require compromises.",
